1
00:00:00,343 --> 00:00:03,763
(Past Howard:)I haven't seen your Oreos!

2
00:00:03,972 --> 00:00:07,062
(Past Howard:)Just take your bath without them!

3
00:00:10,895 --> 00:00:12,355
(Penny:)So why was it his lucky day?

4
00:00:12,522 --> 00:00:15,152
(Leonard:)It turns out I had a little rocket fuel
in the apartment.

5
00:00:15,316 --> 00:00:17,856
(Penny:)What were you doing with
rocket fuel in your apartment?

6
00:00:18,027 --> 00:00:20,487
Joyce Kim was curious
about what I did for a living...

7
00:00:20,655 --> 00:00:23,365
...and I was gonna
kind of show it to her.

8
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:28,540
(Leonard:)The point is, the guys and I
went back to the apartment.

9
00:00:28,705 --> 00:00:32,415
-Are we ever gonna get to the elevator?
-We're close. We're at the apartment.

10
00:00:32,583 --> 00:00:36,133
(Past Leonard:)The trick is to mix it into Tovex in
order to create a combustible gel...

11
00:00:36,295 --> 00:00:39,425
(Past Leonard:)...that will generate over
8000 kilonewtons of thrust.

12
00:00:39,590 --> 00:00:40,760
(Past Raj:)-Cool.
-Nice.

13
00:00:40,925 --> 00:00:42,555
SHELDON:
Won't work.

14
00:00:43,261 --> 00:00:45,721
(Past Leonard:)Excuse me, but I've been
working on this a long time.

15
00:00:45,888 --> 00:00:47,218
(Past Leonard:)Trust me, it'll work.

16
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:49,180
(Past Sheldon:)You don't see your mistake, do you?

17
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:50,770
(Past Leonard:)There's no mistake.

18
00:00:50,935 --> 00:00:53,565
This is for a full scale rocket,
not a model.

19
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:57,400
(Past Leonard:)-Well, I've adjusted the formula.
-Not correctly.

20
00:00:57,567 --> 00:00:59,397
(Past Leonard:)Okay, I've had it with you.

